{"lines": ["Two bodies lay under a Siberian pine, beside the remains of a small fire. Branches above were broken as high as five metres.", "Three more were found between the pine and the tent, in poses that suggested they were heading back.", "The last four were found in May, under four metres of snow in a ravine. Three had fatal injuries. One had major skull damage, two had major chest fractures. A forensic doctor, Boris Vozrozhdenny, said the force would be comparable to a car crash. Yet there were no external wounds.", "Six of the nine died of hypothermia.", "In May 1959 the Soviet inquest concluded that a compelling natural force had killed them. The files went to a secret archive.", "The case was reopened in 2019. In July 2020, a prosecutor, Andrey Kuryakov, announced an avalanche as the official cause. And in 2021, researchers at ETH Zurich and EPFL published a simulation, in Communications Earth and Environment, showing a small slab of wind-blown snow above the tent could explain the injuries.", "Criticisms remain. No avalanche debris was recorded, and critics note that other expeditions in the area did not report such conditions.", "Rule three. The first answer is not the last one, and the last one may still be argued."], "words": [["Two", 0.0, 0.12], ["bodies", 0.12, 0.42], ["lay", 0.42, 0.78], ["under", 0.78, 1.06], ["a", 1.06, 1.18], ["Siberian", 1.18, 1.64], ["pine,", 1.64, 2.04], ["beside", 2.04, 2.66], ["the", 2.66, 2.94], ["remains", 2.94, 3.22], ["of", 3.22, 3.58], ["a", 3.58, 3.66], ["small", 3.66, 3.94], ["fire.", 3.94, 4.48], ["Branches", 4.94, 5.34], ["above", 5.34, 5.64], ["were", 5.64, 5.92], ["broken", 5.92, 6.18], ["as", 6.18, 6.46], ["high", 6.46, 6.72], ["as", 6.72, 6.98], ["five", 6.98, 7.24], ["metres.", 7.24, 8.46], ["Three", 8.46, 8.74], ["more", 8.74, 8.98], ["were", 8.98, 9.2], ["found", 9.2, 9.48], ["between", 9.48, 9.78], ["the", 9.78, 9.96], ["pine", 9.96, 10.18], ["and", 10.18, 10.54], ["the", 10.54, 10.64], ["tent,", 10.64, 10.86